      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Getting some feedback following this Canny which has been really helpful:\n\"The Maximum Resolution field in the VRC AVPro Video Player component only comes into play when the URL supports multiple resolutions.\"\nThis is important to know, as some services such as YouTube and Twitch (with transcoding) will be affected by this.\nFrom what I can tell, the limitation to only receiving 720p from YouTube (even with higher resolutions availabe) appears to be how ytdlp interacts with the video. You can confirm what formats are available with a video running the program with -F flag, where it should confirm that that 720p non-DASH is marked as \"(best)\" available. So by default ytdlp will obtain the \"best\" format it sees.\nThese behaviours seem to largely unaffect simple static file hosting of .mp4 files or stream relay services such as VRCDN.\nFor example, having played back a 2160p video hosted on Discord with untrusted URLS enabled in VRChat, I can confirm a high level of detail on a gigantic video screen in a test world is present.\nAdditionally when streaming back the same 2160p video across VRCDN at their maximum bitrate, I can also see the same high level of detail on the same screen. So far so good!",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
    {
