      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Further tests this time with Twitch.\nI am able to successfully play a stream that is 1080p@30fps only (no transcoding) in my Video Test world that supports a Maximum Resolution of 2160p in both the Unity and AVPro components.\nSetting the Max Resolution to 720 and then trying this test again I receive \"Invalid URL\", so even though there is one resolution option available, this parameter still restricts Twitch from working.\nGoing back to VRCDN tests, I can play back streams in any resolution regardless of what the Maximum Resolution field is configured as.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "62ac553c2c7a981f22cc4e46",
      "author": {
        "_id": "5e8c2e14af4a860606a60ca3",
