      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "In conclusion I think there is some avenues for education here that can be provided.\nIt is reasonable to assume that the default setting of 720 for maximum resolution in the VRC AVPro Video Player component is getting overlooked and restricts Twitch streaming.\nAlso YouTube videos always coming back with 720p as the best option for the video stream is also creating a perception.\nAs the two likeliest largest sources of static and streaming video, this may be creating the preconception that 720p is only supported.\nAs VRCDN and other alternative platforms become more widespread in popularity, this will eventually become less of an issue.\nHowever it may be worth noting in the VRChat documentation that there are some caveats to some of the whitelisted services that cause different user experiences.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
