      "parentID": "62ac53fc2ccb170ba2cc6fc7",
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "62ab1b64b3a6400bb37eee0d",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Pardon the necro, but to expand for posterity and completeness for anyone else who runs across this canny:\n\nThe reason that VRCDN links are considered valid for even 720 maxres, is because those links do not report resolution size back to YTDL, whereas twitch DOES. \n\nSo for twitch, when the returned stream res options are only higher than the max res, it discards those links as options. \n\nFor VRCDN, the lack of res returns it as UNKNOWN which ytdl doesn't discard for any maxres.\n\nIf no urls remain after the maxres discard, the url resolve fails.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
