  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-06-16T12:00:36.635Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Windows Media Foundation should support higher than the current resolution of 720p that is restricted by VRChat today.\nhttps://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/medfound/h-264-video-decoder\n> Windows 7 = 1920 x 1088 \n> Windows 10 = 4096 x 2304 (max guaranteed resolution for DXVA acceleration is 1920 × 1088)\nGiven this, are you able to increase maximum resolution to 1080p with the AVPro component?\nThe result would be vastly improved experiences in the majority of club/festival worlds for UVMapping visuals, more space for data (VRSL, ShaderMotion), and any other video channel content.",
